							<span style="FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: 'Times New Roman'"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: 'Times New Roman'"> <p style="TEXT-ALIGN: center" align="center"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 16pt; FONT-FAMILY: 'Lucida Blackletter'; mso-bidi-font-size: 13.5pt"><img src="/pics/1602/untitled.GIF" /></span></p></span></span><span style="FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: 'Times New Roman'"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: 'Times New Roman'"> <p align="center"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: 'Bradley Hand ITC'; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-bidi-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-ansi-language: EN-US; mso-fareast-language: EN-US; mso-bidi-language: AR-SA"><span style="mso-spacerun: yes"><a href="/custom.aspx?pid=1543"></a></span></span></p><span style="FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: 'Bradley Hand ITC'; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-bidi-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-ansi-language: EN-US; mso-fareast-language: EN-US; mso-bidi-language: AR-SA"><span style="mso-spacerun: yes"> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; TEXT-ALIGN: center" align="center"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 20pt; FONT-FAMILY: 'Celtic Garamond the 2nd'; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 18pt; FONT-FAMILY: 'Celtic Garamond the 2nd'; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-bidi-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-ansi-language: EN-US; mso-fareast-language: EN-US; mso-bidi-language: AR-SA"><font color="#0000ff">A Tale from Norrath</font></span><?xml:namespace prefix = o ns = "urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office" /><o:p></o:p></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; TEXT-ALIGN: center" align="center"><span style="FONT-FAMILY: 'Celtic Garamond the 2nd'">&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p> <h1 style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt" align="center"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 16pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt"><font face="Celtic Garamond the 2nd" color="#0000ff"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 16pt; FONT-FAMILY: 'Celtic Garamond the 2nd'; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-bidi-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-ansi-language: EN-US; mso-fareast-language: EN-US; mso-bidi-language: AR-SA">Binded Souls</span></font></span><font face="Times New Roman">&nbsp;</font></h1> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 16pt; FONT-FAMILY: Magik; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt"></span>&nbsp;</p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 16pt; FONT-FAMILY: Magik; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt">Long ago, Rikov the<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>warrior yearned for something. He was a vivacious Froglok whose wit and determination were unmatched.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>His froggie ambitions brought him, in his youth, to Kurns Tower.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>There, he made friends, some kindred spirits so to speak.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>Together, with Enyar, Veular, Melyki, Noetikos, Norlath, Krigan, Hanso, Mynok and others he created Binded Souls.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>Rikov had found that which he longed for, a family.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>Binded Souls was a family, a place without the strict rules of many guilds.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>A place where helping one another was commonplace, a place to relax and socialize with your friends.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>It became a home.<o:p></o:p></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 16pt; FONT-FAMILY: Magik; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt">&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 16pt; FONT-FAMILY: Magik; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt">As the bind grew, new faces were introduced.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>Among them was that of Panndaabear.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>Panda was a kind soul, with a lust for life that was endearing.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>A good listener, Panda knew the truth behind all secrets amongst the guild.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span><o:p></o:p></span></p> <p style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 16pt; FONT-FAMILY: Magik; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-bidi-font-family: 'Times New Roman'">&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 16pt; FONT-FAMILY: Magik; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt">Another new face was that of Amyana.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>Noetikos, along with Valerene discovered the young high elf in the Faydark below Kelethin.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>Noetikos, a witty wood elf, liked her bubbly ways, and invited her to join their family. <o:p></o:p></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 16pt; FONT-FAMILY: Magik; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt">&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 16pt; FONT-FAMILY: Magik; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt">The queen of the Bind, Rikov’s queen was Valerene.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>Reigning from her throne in the field of bone, Valerene was a just queen.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>She cared deeply for her people, and took care of them.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>She took Amyana under her wing, and showed her the ways of Norrath. Noetikos and Amyana quickly formed a friendship.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>They understood one another and became dear friends.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>Amyana admired the elder elven man, he was intelligent, patient and charming.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>Rikov seemed to like the little elf as well, and promoted her to an officer within the guild.</span><span style="FONT-FAMILY: Arabolical"> </span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"><font face="Times New Roman">&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></font></p> <p style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; TEXT-ALIGN: center" align="center"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 16pt; FONT-FAMILY: 'Celtic Garamond the 2nd'; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-bidi-font-family: 'Times New Roman'"><font color="#0000ff">The New Guild<o:p></o:p></font></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"><font face="Times New Roman">&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></font></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 16pt; FONT-FAMILY: Magik; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt">Rikov vanished.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>Binded Souls worried about their leader.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>They had no idea where he had gone off too.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>It was rumored that he had forsaken them, and people became restless.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>There was a fear that people would leave, and join other guilds of Norrath.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>In order to keep the guild together, Amyana created Moonlite Redemption.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>Several members of Binded Souls broke away from Binded Souls and joined Moonlite Redemption.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span><o:p></o:p></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 16pt; FONT-FAMILY: Magik; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt">&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 16pt; FONT-FAMILY: Magik; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt">Among the last to leave Binded, was Noetikos.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>He was loyal to Rikov, and was faced with a difficult decision.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>In time, Noetikos and Amyana became co-leaders of the guild; they complimented each other well, and made a good team.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>Among the original members of Moonlite Redemption were Chukasna, Weic, Gaanndolff, Urmezzmerized, Uanelil, and Ayteyex.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>Together, they made Moonlite Redemption a respectable, lovable guild.</span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"><font face="Times New Roman">&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></font></p> <p style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; TEXT-ALIGN: center" align="center"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 16pt; FONT-FAMILY: 'Celtic Garamond the 2nd'; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-bidi-font-family: 'Times New Roman'"><font color="#0000ff">Rikov's Return<o:p></o:p></font></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"><font face="Times New Roman">&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></font></p> <p class="MsoBodyText" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"><font face="Magik" size="5">Rikov returned to Norrath.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>It was discovered that he had not forsaken his people; he had been unable to return due to forces beyond his control!<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>His guild, his family was gone, it was too late, the damage was done. He has a big heart, and felt no anger toward his friends.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>Eventually, Rikov sadly disbanded Binded Souls and re-joined his friends in Moonlite Redemption.</font></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"><font face="Times New Roman">&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></font></p> <p style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; TEXT-ALIGN: center" align="center"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 16pt; FONT-FAMILY: 'Celtic Garamond the 2nd'; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-bidi-font-family: 'Times New Roman'"><font color="#0000ff">The Bind lives on<o:p></o:p></font></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 16pt; FONT-FAMILY: Magik; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt">&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 16pt; FONT-FAMILY: Magik; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt">Many of the original bind have moved on, or even away from Norrath altogether.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>Several of the bind are now in Moonlite Redemption.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>Moonlite Redemption holds many of the same ideals as the Binded Souls, and so, in a way, Binded Souls lives on in this guild.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>Binded Souls breathed the first whisper of life into Moonlite Redemption, and made it possible, and shall always be cherished for this.</span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"><font face="Times New Roman">&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></font></p> <p style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; TEXT-ALIGN: center" align="center"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 16pt; FONT-FAMILY: 'Celtic Garamond the 2nd'; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-bidi-font-family: 'Times New Roman'"><font color="#0000ff">Moonlite Redemption<o:p></o:p></font></span></p> <p style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"><span style="FONT-FAMILY: 'Viner Hand ITC'; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-bidi-font-family: 'Times New Roman'">&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p> <p align="left"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 16pt; FONT-FAMILY: Magik; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-bidi-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-ansi-language: EN-US; mso-fareast-language: EN-US; mso-bidi-language: AR-SA">Moonlite Redemption’s goal is to be a family raiding guild.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>Members of the guild treat each other like family, they care about one another.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>Every family has bickering, but their love for one another gets them through it.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>Even though they are a family guild, they raid together somewhat frequently, banishing as much evil from Norrath as they are able.&nbsp; Although the term evil is relative.&nbsp; </span></p> <p align="center"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 16pt; FONT-FAMILY: Magik; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-bidi-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-ansi-language: EN-US; mso-fareast-language: EN-US; mso-bidi-language: AR-SA">We live, we love, we die, this is our way.&nbsp; </span></p> <p align="center"><a href="/custom.aspx?pid=1543"><em></em></a>&nbsp;</p></span></span></span></span>
							
